{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Settings\/defaultWindowPlacement(_:)"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/settings\/defaultwindowplacement(_:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultWindowPlacement"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"makePlacement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@escaping "},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI16WindowLayoutRootV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WindowLayoutRoot","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowLayoutRoot"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowPlacementContext","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI22WindowPlacementContextV","text":"WindowPlacementContext"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowPlacement","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI15WindowPlacementV","text":"WindowPlacement"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP","text":"Scene"},{"kind":"text","text":"\n"}]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A closure to generate the default window placement.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"makePlacement"}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this scene modifier to indicate a default initial size and position","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for a new window that the system creates from a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" declaration."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On Windows, you can use the screen’s bounds to place the window."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example, you can specify that the window is always placed 140"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"points from the bottom of the screen:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["struct MyApp: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        ...","","        Window(\"Status\", id: \"status\") {","            StatusView()","        }","        .windowResizability(.contentSize)","        .defaultWindowPlacement { content, context in","            let displayBounds = context.defaultDisplay.visibleRect","            let size = content.sizeThatFits(.unspecified)","            let position = CGPoint(","                x: displayBounds.midX - (size.width \/ 2),","                y: displayBounds.maxY - size.height - 140)","            return WindowPlacement(position: position, size: size)","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On visionOS, the system always places the first window"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative to where the person is looking."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The system ignores calls to "},{"code":"defaultWindowPlacement(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can place any subsequent windows relative to existing ones by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returning one of the methods defined by "},{"code":"WindowPlacement\/Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the existing window.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"For example, you can align the new window with the trailing edge of"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content"},{"type":"text","text":" window:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["struct MyApp: App {","    @Environment(\\.openWindow) private var openWindow","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup(\"Content\", id: \"content\") {","            Button(\"Open status window\") {","                openWindow(id: \"status\")","            }","        }","","        WindowGroup(\"Status\", id: \"status\") {","            StatusView()","        }","        .windowResizability(.contentSize)","        .defaultWindowPlacement { content, context in","            if let contentWindow = context.windows.first(","            where: { $0.id == \"content\" }) {","                WindowPlacement(.trailing(contentWindow))","            } else {","                WindowPlacement()","            }","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement that your function returns acts as a default for when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"window first appears. People can later resize and move the window using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interface controls that the system provides. Also, during state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restoration, the system restores the window to it’s most recent size and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position, rather than the default placement."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For more information on configuring how scenes behave with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state restoration, see ","type":"text"},{"code":"Scene.stateRestoration(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Settings"]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultWindowPlacement","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"((","kind":"text"},{"text":"WindowLayoutRoot","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI16WindowLayoutRootV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WindowPlacementContext","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI22WindowPlacementContextV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WindowPlacement","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI15WindowPlacementV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Scene","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"title":"defaultWindowPlacement(_:)","role":"symbol","extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5ScenePAAE22defaultWindowPlacementyQrAA0fG0VAA0F10LayoutRootV_AA0fG7ContextVtcF::SYNTHESIZED::s:11OpenSwiftUI8SettingsV"},"abstract":[{"text":"Defines a function used for determining the default placement","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of windows.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Settings/defaultWindowPlacement(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/settings\/defaultwindowplacement(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Settings\/defaultWindowPlacement(_:)","title":"defaultWindowPlacement(_:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Defines a function used for determinin